+# E2E Test Guide — `Routing guide, core files and issue templates` (`5.0.0`)
+
+- **Capability:** `/sc:help` lists what is installed and prints the six-level table from the routing guide `~/.claude/HOW-WE-WORK.md`, or an exact fallback line when the guide is missing or broken; `/sc:recommend` reads that guide first and returns the matching routing row's steps; 5.0.0 ships 11 core files (including `ISSUE-HANDOFF.md` and `ISSUE-BACKLOG.md`) and no longer ships `/sc:README`, the `/ccsession-tag` command or six old core files; the shipped `CLAUDE.md` tells Claude to file GitHub issues from a filled copy of an issue template, never from the template itself.
+- **Audience:** end user
+- **Source of truth:** `src/superclaude/commands/help.md:21-93,132`; `src/superclaude/commands/recommend.md:32-60`; `src/superclaude/skills/sc-recommend/SKILL.md:290`; `src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md:11-28,350-354`; `src/superclaude/cli/install_core.py:13-27`; `src/superclaude/cli/install_commands.py:11,39-40,142-144`; `src/superclaude/core/ISSUE-HANDOFF.md`, `src/superclaude/core/ISSUE-BACKLOG.md`; `src/superclaude/core/CLAUDE.md:43`; `src/superclaude/skills/ccsession-tag/SKILL.md:1-5`; `CHANGELOG.md:43-44,70,244,248,252`; `docs/testing/v5.0.0/c-e2e-transcript.txt:380-389`
+- **Est. time:** `Tier A: 2 minutes. Tier B: 1 minute. Tier C: 25-35 minutes in interactive Claude Code sessions, plus 5 minutes for the optional [EXTERNAL] issue steps.`
+
+## Preconditions
+
+- IronClaude 5.0.0 installed for your user (`superclaude install` done): `superclaude --version` prints `SuperClaude, version 5.0.0`.
+- `git` and the `claude` CLI on your `PATH`, and a Claude Code login for Tier C (each Tier C step uses API tokens). Steps 13-15 also need `gh` logged in to a GitHub account where you may create a throwaway private repository.
+- `/tmp/d05` does not exist (`[ ! -e /tmp/d05 ] && echo OK` prints `OK`). Every file this guide creates is under `/tmp/d05`. No step moves, edits or deletes anything under your real `~/.claude`; Step 5 records checksums of the files this guide reads and Step 16 checks they are unchanged. Tier C sessions still write to your real `~/.claude` in two ways no step controls: Claude Code saves each session's history, and the hooks that `superclaude install` registers write state and log files under `~/.claude/state/` and `~/.claude/logs/` at session start and on each prompt (`src/superclaude/hooks/hooks.json:18,49`; `src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/freshness-session-start.sh:8-9`, `freshness-user-prompt.sh:8-10`, `auggie-flag-clear.sh:10-12`). The Step 5 and Step 16 checksums do not cover those two folders.
+- Run every `/sc:help` and `/sc:recommend` step outside an IronClaude checkout (the steps use `/tmp/d05/...`). Inside a checkout, both commands read the checkout's `src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md` before the installed copy (`src/superclaude/commands/help.md:67`; `src/superclaude/commands/recommend.md:44`), which is a different file from the one under test.
+- `/sc:help` and `/sc:recommend` are carried out by Claude following the command files; there is no script behind them. Expected results give the exact lines the command file fixes and judge the rest on content, not wording.
+
+## What you're verifying
+
+- `/sc:help` lists the installed commands and skills read from disk (a command with no `description:` line shows `(no description line)`, `-protocol` skills come last), prints the guide's level table and hard limit verbatim, names the two Claude Code built-ins, points to the guide and to `/sc:recommend`, and writes nothing.
+- With no guide it prints the exact "Routing guide not found" line; with a guide that lacks the markers it prints the exact "has no level table" line.
+- `/sc:recommend` routes a one-file rename to level 2 and a multi-file feature to level 3 (`/sc:workflow`, then `/sc:implement` only when execution is requested), changes no file, and warns and ignores `--minstar` without `--plugin`.
+- The removed surface is absent: no `/sc:README` in a new install, no user-invocable `/ccsession-tag`, none of `ORCHESTRATOR.md`, `COMMANDS.md`, `PERSONAS.md`, `MODES.md`, `FLAGS.md`, `MCP.md` among the shipped core files.
+- `~/.claude/ISSUE-HANDOFF.md` and `~/.claude/ISSUE-BACKLOG.md` exist with four `##` headings each, and asking Claude to file a backlog issue uses a filled copy and leaves the template byte-for-byte unchanged.
